docs/D435I_BASELINE_AUDIT.md:75:The D435i was on the USB 2.x path despite a USB 3.x root hub existing. SDK reports USB type `2.1`. Host `/dev/video0..5` were `root:video`, mode `0660` with an ACL marker. Camera HID was `/dev/hidraw3`, `root:root`, `0600`; its sysfs path contains `5-3:1.5/0003:8086:0B3A.0004`. Other hidraw devices are QEMU tablets. No IIO device names were enumerated; `/sys/bus/iio/devices` was empty at final inspection. Kernel logged hid-sensor-hub report-ID warnings during root camera startup. At this initial inspection the live SDK IMU backend was unproven. The resumed non-root failure identifies the HID/IIO sysfs scan-control path (section 16); hidraw permissions alone do not establish the SDK's access requirements.
