+++ b/experiments/2026-10-13-n4b-d435i-prep/n4b_plan.md
@@ -0,0 +1,362 @@
+# N4B offline and N4C live — OPEN
+
+Prepared on the Mac only. No camera, SDK process, ORB executable, SSH, network,
+installation, commit or push was run. Every gate is **OPEN**. Commands below
+are future **local Pi terminal** instructions, not evidence of execution.
+
+## Shortest credible sequence
+
+1. Finish the already initiated native Pi build in `~/orbslam3/ORB_SLAM3`.
+   Pangolin 0.9.1 / C++17 and that path are supplied task context, not newly
+   verified artifacts. Preserve native build fixes/logs; inspect compiler/link
+   flags, source identity and library hashes once the build finishes.
+2. After the user explicitly says **CAMERA AVAILABLE**, requalify the new unit
+   using [Phase A N1→N2→N3](../2026-09-12-pi5-native-sensor-validation/PHASE_A_RUNBOOK.md).
+   [NEXT_GATE](../../docs/NEXT_GATE.md) still identifies N3; this proposal does
+   not advance it or waive it. Old-unit receipts do not transfer. Fresh N1 must
+   select SDK `317422076650` and separately attest descriptor `327743061057`,
+   USB **≥5000M**, permissions, stable power/cooling and actual topology.
+   Correct old hard-coded SDK selection in a separately reviewed runtime bundle.
+3. N2 stays **IR1 Y8 640×480/15, gyro/200, accel/100**, native raw streams,
+   20 s → 105 s → mandatory **300 s soak**. Keep all timing thresholds: IR
+   14.25–15.75 Hz, gyro 190–210, accel 95–105, image gaps ≤0.20 s, motion gaps
+   ≤0.05 s, positive stamp/frame steps, no missing image frame numbers, original
+   health/fault criteria and raw logs. Qualify separate dataset storage before
+   recording; take fresh N1 after its qualification. Complete the unresolved N3
+   record/replay and timing evidence without live/replay contamination.
+4. Build this isolated example and recorder against the completed native
+   libraries. Capture a **60–90 s** guided take with both IR streams **30 Hz**,
+   gyro **200 Hz**, accel **100 Hz**, emitter OFF, no other camera process.
+   This is an additional N4 development profile, not a replacement N2 profile.
+   Attest actual stereo delivery and timing independently at 30 Hz.
+5. Finalize/hash the librealsense bag and logs. Inspect decoded IR pixels,
+   stream inventory, counts, domains, motion and boundary coverage. Run the
+   same driver with `--bag ... --no-viewer` for N4B. Repeat on the identical
+   immutable bag and YAML; preserve all failures and run-specific outputs.
+6. Only after review of N4B input/initialization/tracking evidence, use that
+   binary and YAML without `--bag` for N4C. Measure live processing, dropped
+   frames, health and latency. Neither milestone constitutes calibrated VIO
+   accuracy. Allan variance, IMU intrinsic/extrinsic and temporal calibration
+   remain prerequisites to N4 qualification.
+
+## One input path and exact profiles
+
+The [unapplied patch](stereo_inertial_d435i_file.patch) targets only
+`Examples/Stereo-Inertial/stereo_inertial_realsense_D435i.cc` at
+`4452a3c4ab75b1cde34e5505a36ec3f9edcdc4c4`. Copy the two supporting headers
+[d435i_input.h](d435i_input.h) and [d435i_rs.h](d435i_rs.h) alongside the patched
+example. No core algorithm, System API, CMake file, node graph or custom dataset
+format change is proposed. This replaces the example's fragile acquisition
+section; merely adding two flags would leave known input errors in place.
+The original GPL notice remains on the patched source.
+
+- `--bag FILE` uses `rs2::config::enable_device_from_file(FILE,false)` (no
+  looping). Resolve the recorded device without querying physical cameras and
+  set `rs2::playback::set_real_time(false)` **before** pipeline start. The file
+  branch does not write live sensor options and does not substitute arrival
+  time for recorded timestamps. Disconnecting the camera is a useful future
+  file-only validation after CAMERA AVAILABLE, not a present requirement.
+- `--no-viewer` supplies `false` to the existing System viewer argument. The
+  default still enables it. Headless runtime still links Pangolin because the
+  upstream library and included headers require it.
+- Both branches explicitly select IR1/IR2 **Y8 640×480/30**, gyro
+  **MOTION_XYZ32F/200**, accel **MOTION_XYZ32F/100** and verify the resolved
+  profiles and SDK serial. No depth/RGB stream or rate fallback is allowed.
+  The new enumeration lists accel **400/200/100**, gyro **400/200**; **250 Hz
+  is not supported by this unit's readback**. The upstream example explicitly
+  requests IR/30 but leaves both motion rates unspecified; its 200/60 Hz
+  comments are not a capability measurement. IMU.Frequency 200 is the resulting
+  gyro-grid input rate, with bracketed accel interpolation.
+- The shared input helper rejects nonfinite and duplicate/backward samples,
+  rejects interior motion gaps >50 ms, and interpolates only inside valid accel
+  brackets. It sends gyro samples through the first timestamp at/after each
+  image, once; pinned `Tracking.cc` retains this final endpoint internally.
+  Uncovered startup gyros/images and EOF images are explicitly counted. A
+  useful dataset needs enough leading/trailing coverage; discarded boundaries
+  are reviewed, not hidden as a clean run.
+- Own cloned image pixels with SDK row strides, preserve image order in an
+  eight-pair queue (≈4.92 MB pixels), bound motion queues, and fix the upstream
+  interpolation overwrite. Playback waits for queue space; live overload
+  fails explicitly. No silent latest-image overwrite. A 10 s backpressure
+  timeout, 5 s coverage timeout and ≤1 ms pair-skew guard are **development
+  guards**, not changes to N1/N2 or calibrated synchronization thresholds.
+- Load vocabulary before starting capture; handle EOF/SIGINT/SIGTERM; stop
+  pipeline, shut down SLAM and save trajectories into fresh run directories.
+  SDK integration/EOF/callback scheduling still needs real-file validation.
+  Non-real-time playback does not make SLAM's mapping threads deterministic;
+  compare repeated runs and keep state/reset histories.
+
+[d435i_record.cpp](d435i_record.cpp) uses `enable_record_to_file`, exclusive new
+output directory, a bounded duration (1–120 s), callbacks for all four selected
+streams, full-precision timestamp/IMU audit CSV and normal stop/finalization.
+The SDK handles bag serialization. The callback counts are observations at the
+application layer; they do not establish that every hardware sample was stored.
+Reconcile stored-frame decode counts and timestamp steps against them.
+
+Emitter OFF is set/read back before live streaming in both programs. Projector
+dots are actively projected texture whose motion/view dependence can break
+stereo feature tracking and temporal feature identity. Use real, static scene
+texture and diffuse light. Disabling the emitter is a runtime stream option,
+not a calibration/firmware write. Exposure, motion-correction and global-time
+settings are preserved; motion-correction/global-time values are logged. Record
+exposure metadata and inspect blur; do not infer calibrated inertial readings
+from motion correction being enabled. Never run recorder and SLAM concurrently.
+
+## Future Pi build in a separate bundle
+
+Use already supplied, checksum-verified Mac files in a fresh Pi runtime bundle;
+transport is outside this Mac-only task. Do not reset/copy over either checkout
+or apply the patch to `~/orbslam3/ORB_SLAM3`. The following reads the existing
+native build's generated compile/link recipes, builds only an isolated example,
+and reuses completed libraries. It introduces no install or full rebuild.
+Stop on any command failure and preserve stdout/stderr; do not hide a missing
+target/dependency. These commands assume the current build uses Unix Makefiles
+and has the RealSense example target; other generators require review.
+
+```bash
+# Future local Pi terminal, after native build completion; CAMERA AVAILABLE
+# is additionally required before any ORB or camera-dependent execution.
+set -euo pipefail
+export WBR_ORB="$HOME/orbslam3/ORB_SLAM3"
+export WBR_PREP="$HOME/wbr-perception-phase1-runtime/experiments/2026-10-13-n4b-d435i-prep"
+export WBR_BUNDLE="$HOME/wbr-runtime/n4b-$(date -u +%Y%m%dT%H%M%SZ)"
+mkdir -p "$HOME/wbr-runtime"
+mkdir "$WBR_BUNDLE"
+cd "$WBR_PREP"
+sha256sum -c SHA256SUMS
+mkdir -p "$WBR_BUNDLE/source/Examples/Stereo-Inertial" "$WBR_BUNDLE/bin"
+cp "$WBR_ORB/Examples/Stereo-Inertial/stereo_inertial_realsense_D435i.cc" \
+   "$WBR_BUNDLE/source/Examples/Stereo-Inertial/"
+cp d435i_input.h d435i_rs.h "$WBR_BUNDLE/source/Examples/Stereo-Inertial/"
+cp d435i_record.cpp d435i_rs.h "$WBR_BUNDLE/source/"
+cp D435i_317422076650_stereo_inertial.yaml "$WBR_BUNDLE/"
+sha256sum "$WBR_ORB/Examples/Stereo-Inertial/stereo_inertial_realsense_D435i.cc"
+# Compare to the pinned source digest printed in verification.md before proceeding.
+patch --dry-run -d "$WBR_BUNDLE/source" -p1 < stereo_inertial_d435i_file.patch
+patch -d "$WBR_BUNDLE/source" -p1 < stereo_inertial_d435i_file.patch
+
+python3 - "$WBR_ORB" "$WBR_BUNDLE" <<'PY'
+from pathlib import Path
+import shlex, subprocess, sys
+orb, bundle = map(lambda s: Path(s).resolve(), sys.argv[1:])
+build = orb/'build'
+target = 'stereo_inertial_realsense_D435i'
+recipe = build/'CMakeFiles'/f'{target}.dir'
+settings = {}
+for line in (recipe/'flags.make').read_text().splitlines():
+    if ' = ' in line:
+        key, value = line.split(' = ', 1)
+        settings[key] = shlex.split(value)
+link = shlex.split((recipe/'link.txt').read_text())
+objects = [i for i, s in enumerate(link) if s.endswith('.o')]
+assert len(objects) == 1, 'review unexpected target link recipe'
+assert link.count('-o') == 1, 'review unexpected output flag'
+flags = sum((settings[k] for k in ('CXX_DEFINES','CXX_INCLUDES','CXX_FLAGS')), [])
+assert '-std=c++17' in flags, 'native C++17 build must complete first'
+obj = bundle/'bin'/f'{target}.o'
+binary = bundle/'bin'/target
+source = bundle/'source/Examples/Stereo-Inertial'/f'{target}.cc'
+compile_cmd = [link[0], *flags, '-c', str(source), '-o', str(obj)]
+link[objects[0]] = str(obj)
+link[link.index('-o')+1] = str(binary)
+for cmd in (compile_cmd, link):
+    print(shlex.join(cmd), flush=True)
+    subprocess.run(cmd, cwd=build, check=True)
+PY
+
+# Use the same already-installed librealsense as ORB; no installation here.
+pkg-config --modversion realsense2
+c++ -std=c++17 -O2 -Wall -Wextra -pthread \
+  $(pkg-config --cflags realsense2) "$WBR_BUNDLE/source/d435i_record.cpp" \
+  -o "$WBR_BUNDLE/bin/d435i_record" $(pkg-config --libs realsense2)
+sha256sum "$WBR_BUNDLE/bin/"* "$WBR_ORB/lib/libORB_SLAM3.so" \
+  "$WBR_ORB/Thirdparty/DBoW2/lib/libDBoW2.so" \
+  "$WBR_ORB/Thirdparty/g2o/lib/libg2o.so" "$WBR_ORB/Vocabulary/ORBvoc.txt" \
+  > "$WBR_BUNDLE/build-sha256.txt"
+ldd "$WBR_BUNDLE/bin/stereo_inertial_realsense_D435i" > "$WBR_BUNDLE/ldd.txt"
+```
+
+Preserve compile/link commands and logs, original CMake cache/flags/link recipe,
+Pi native patches, OS/kernel/compiler, librealsense/Pangolin/OpenCV versions,
+library paths/hashes, vocabulary/config/headers/patch hashes and parent source
+commit. Library paths in the existing recipe refer to the preserved native
+build; retain those libraries for this bundle's lifetime. `pkg-config` must
+select the same SDK used by ORB, not an unrelated installation. `ldd` must have
+no missing libraries. Building remains OPEN until compiled on the Pi.
+
+## Storage and a future recording command
+
+IR payload per pair is `2*640*480*1=614,400 B`. At 30 Hz that is **18.432 MB/s**,
+**1.10592 GB/min = 1.02997 GiB/min**. Gyro/200 + accel/100 raw XYZ floats add
+`300*12*60=216,000 B/min` before timestamps, serialization and metadata. Audit
+CSV adds roughly a few MB/min depending on metadata. Bag indexing, overhead,
+compression behavior, recorder backlog and peak write speed are **UNKNOWN**.
+Budget **1.5 GB/min** provisionally; measure finalized file size and peak writes.
+90 s is ≈1.659 GB pixels alone; 300 s stereo is ≈5.530 GB pixels alone.
+
+The [snapshot](../2026-10-13-pi5-env-snapshot/CODEX_INSPECTION.md) measured about
+**17 GiB available before build** on a nominal 32 GB microSD. Even ignoring all
+overhead this is only ≈16.5 min; with a provisional 5 GiB OS reserve and 1.5
+GB/min budget it is ≈8.6 min **before subtracting build/swap growth**. Those are
+arithmetic limits, not capture authorization. The build script may add a 4 GiB
+swap file. Recheck `df -B1`, swap and build sizes. Repository policy keeps
+microSD for OS/tools/small logs; GB-scale bags and Allan recordings require
+separately qualified storage. No fallback to a directory on `/` is proposed.
+
+```bash
+# Future Pi only: mount/storage qualification, new-unit N1/N2/N3 and
+# CAMERA AVAILABLE must already be documented. Substitute the actually
+# qualified mount; merely creating this directory does not qualify storage.
+export WBR_DATA=/mnt/wbr-qualified-data
+findmnt -T "$WBR_DATA" -o SOURCE,TARGET,FSTYPE,OPTIONS
+df -B1 "$WBR_DATA"
+swapon --show
+test "$(findmnt -n -o SOURCE -T "$WBR_DATA")" != "$(findmnt -n -o SOURCE -T /)"
+test "$(df -B1 --output=avail "$WBR_DATA" | tail -1)" -gt 3221225472
+mkdir -p "$WBR_DATA/n4b"
+export WBR_TAKE="$WBR_DATA/n4b/take-$(date -u +%Y%m%dT%H%M%SZ)"
+# Recorder creates WBR_TAKE exclusively; tee log stays outside until it exists.
+set -o pipefail
+"$WBR_BUNDLE/bin/d435i_record" "$WBR_TAKE" 90 \
+  2>&1 | tee "$WBR_DATA/n4b/$(basename "$WBR_TAKE")-record.log"
+sha256sum "$WBR_TAKE/stereo_imu.bag" "$WBR_TAKE/timestamps.csv" \
+  > "$WBR_TAKE/SHA256SUMS"
+du -B1 "$WBR_TAKE/stereo_imu.bag"
+```
+
+Monitor free space, continuous kernel logs, power/temperature/CPU/RSS while
+recording; normal SIGINT handles a fault and finalizes the partial bag. Preserve
+that partial take and classify it. Never kill -9 to make the duration fit.
+The tiny recorder neither qualifies mounts nor monitors health by itself;
+reuse the existing gate/health tooling with a reviewed new-unit selection.
+Qualified storage must sustain more than the 18.432 MB/s payload plus measured
+overhead with margin; apply the storage runbook and review against this profile.
+
+## Hand motion for initialization
+
+Keep the Pi stationary and cool. Move **the camera** with cable slack and strain
+relief; do not rock the USB/power connector. Face a well-lit scene with static,
+nonrepeating texture at several depths, avoiding blank walls, mirrors and
+moving people. Within the first 1–2 s begin smooth translation, so a long
+stationary prefix does not provoke an initialization reset.
+
+For the next **20–30 s**, translate left/right, up/down and forward/back roughly
+10–30 cm, mixing changes in speed with slow/moderate roll, pitch and yaw
+roughly ±15–30°. Keep texture visible in both IR views, avoid blur, sudden
+impacts, rapid spins, pure rotation and constant-velocity planar-only motion.
+Then continue a small room loop for **30–50 s**, revisit the original view and
+end with **5–10 s stationary**. A 60–90 s take gives initialization and refinement
+time; it is not a duration-based guarantee. A separately planned stationary
+calibration record may use a stationary prefix; this VIO take prioritizes early
+excitation. It is not a Kalibr target dataset or Allan-variance experiment.
+
+Pinned `LocalMapping::InitializeIMU` requires ≥10 keyframes and ≥1 s stereo
+keyframe span before attempting initialization. Insufficient translation can
+print `Not enough motion for initializing. Reseting...`; early initialization
+is followed by refinement around accumulated motion times >5 s and >15 s.
+These are algorithm conditions, not promises that a one-second take suffices.
+
+## Future N4B and N4C commands and observations
+
+```bash
+# Future N4B, only after input evidence review and CAMERA AVAILABLE.
+# Stop all live camera publishers/recorders first. Same binary/YAML for both modes.
+export LD_LIBRARY_PATH="$WBR_ORB/lib:$WBR_ORB/Thirdparty/DBoW2/lib:$WBR_ORB/Thirdparty/g2o/lib${LD_LIBRARY_PATH:+:$LD_LIBRARY_PATH}"
+export WBR_RUN="$WBR_DATA/n4b/offline-$(date -u +%Y%m%dT%H%M%SZ)"
+mkdir "$WBR_RUN"
+cd "$WBR_RUN"
+sha256sum "$WBR_TAKE/stereo_imu.bag" \
+  "$WBR_BUNDLE/D435i_317422076650_stereo_inertial.yaml" > inputs.sha256
+set -o pipefail
+/usr/bin/time -v "$WBR_BUNDLE/bin/stereo_inertial_realsense_D435i" \
+  "$WBR_ORB/Vocabulary/ORBvoc.txt" \
+  "$WBR_BUNDLE/D435i_317422076650_stereo_inertial.yaml" n4b \
+  --bag "$WBR_TAKE/stereo_imu.bag" --no-viewer 2>&1 | tee run.log
+rg -n 'IMU initialized|maps in the atlas|Creation of new map|Not enough motion|LOST|lost|reset|Reseting|OPEN:' run.log
+
+# Future N4C: review N4B first; live health logging and guided motion required.
+export WBR_RUN="$WBR_DATA/n4b/live-$(date -u +%Y%m%dT%H%M%SZ)"
+mkdir "$WBR_RUN"
+cd "$WBR_RUN"
+set -o pipefail
+timeout --signal=INT --kill-after=30s 90s \
+  "$WBR_BUNDLE/bin/stereo_inertial_realsense_D435i" \
+  "$WBR_ORB/Vocabulary/ORBvoc.txt" \
+  "$WBR_BUNDLE/D435i_317422076650_stereo_inertial.yaml" n4c \
+  --no-viewer 2>&1 | tee run.log
+# timeout normally returns 124: preserve it and review normal shutdown logs;
+# forced KILL or missing finalization is a failed attempt, never a success.
+```
+
+Preserve each exit status (`pipefail`), log and output hash. Proposed observations
+for a **reviewable development run**, all currently OPEN:
+
+- Correct four profiles, SDK identity, paired readable IR pixels; full source
+  and config provenance. Bag decode must reconcile recorded raw counts/stamps
+  against recorder CSV and driver input audit. No missing interior frame numbers,
+  nonfinite/reversed stamps, unexplained large gaps or mixed/changing domains.
+  Tiny boundary exclusions must be reported and explained, not called lossless.
+- See atlas creation, actual keyframes and initialization/refinement logs.
+  The literal `IMU initialized` line is **added by this patch**, tied to the
+  existing `System::GetTimeFromIMUInit()>0`; stock pinned code sets the internal
+  flag without that literal line. It is not a hard-coded success announcement.
+  `*_tracking.csv` records its per-frame value, so resets/loss of initialization
+  remain visible. Global BA messages alone do not prove initialization.
+- Track state from `Tracking.h`: -1 SYSTEM_NOT_READY, 0 NO_IMAGES_YET,
+  1 NOT_INITIALIZED, 2 OK, 3 RECENTLY_LOST, 4 LOST, 5 OK_KLT.
+  Inspect 3/4 intervals, reset/new-map messages, state fraction and duration
+  after initialization. For the short controlled first take, target sustained
+  state 2 and one map without repeated resets. Keep failures; an output trajectory
+  or nonzero initialization flag does not establish accuracy.
+- `SaveTrajectoryEuRoC` prints `There are N maps in the atlas` and per-map KF
+  counts. Expect one stable map for the simple take; explain any extras and map
+  switches. The exporter chooses the largest map, so a plausible trajectory can
+  hide losses in other maps. Inspect atlas logs and state timeline alongside it.
+  Require nonempty finite trajectories, monotonic stamps and useful coverage.
+- Review received/processed/prefix/tail/pending counters; no unexplained interior
+  loss or queue error. At 30 Hz live, process an image every ≈33.3 ms on average
+  with bounded backlog; report per-frame processing time, peak RSS and wall/data
+  duration. A file run slower than real time may be useful N4B evidence, but
+  does not qualify N4C throughput. Repeat the same bag before going live.
+- No new power/thermal/USB/kernel faults, forced shutdown or storage exhaustion.
+  Initialization and continuity are development observations; ATE/RPE require
+  reference trajectories and a documented alignment, currently unavailable.
+
+## Frames and timestamps: measured versus unknown
+
+| Stage | Evidence / classification | Remaining OPEN condition |
+|---|---|---|
+| IR1/IR2 optical frames and SDK extrinsics | MEASURED enumeration; see [math](calibration_notes.md) | Physical calibration accuracy, actual pair delivery and exposure timing |
+| IMU gyro/accel frames | MEASURED SDK identity alignment; nominal mechanical interpretation INFERRED | Bias/scale/alignment calibration, true device-specific noise |
+| Hardware acquisition clocks | UNKNOWN for a new streaming interval | Read every stream's domain; do not assume a single clock just from fps |
+| `GLOBAL_TIME_ENABLED` | Old-unit docs report 1; **new-unit state UNKNOWN** | Shared code logs current value and preserves it; compare domains and startup transitions |
+| Global-time mapping | SOURCE-SUPPORTED via repository's SDK global reader citation | Mapping toward host time does not measure exposure-to-IMU time offset; host clock steps/drift remain possible |
+| SDK frame stamps | API gives double milliseconds, saved at 17-digit precision | Capture original stamp/domain/number plus steady/UTC arrival, exposure metadata and full-precision motion |
+| Bag storage/playback | SDK .bag, not a ROS2 rosbag2 directory | Verify stored pixels, metadata and recorded timestamp/domain preservation on installed SDK; no playback wall-time substitution |
+| ORB input | SDK ms ×1e-3 to seconds; left IR stamp used; accel interpolated at gyro stamps | Same ordered domain required; camera–IMU offset UNKNOWN, no invented correction applied |
+| Host arrivals | Audited at callback observation | These include transport, scheduling and logging; subtraction is not pure USB latency |
+| ORB trajectory stamps | Pinned EuRoC exporter multiplies input seconds by 1e9 | Verify domain/units and coverage; do not compare to UTC ground truth without clock characterization |
+
+Preserve domain changes rather than relabeling them. The driver deliberately
+stops on mixed/changing domains; diagnose with the saved partial bag/audit and
+a separately labeled timestamp experiment. An option readback of 1 is not a
+measurement of synchronization. Host global timestamps do not prove hardware
+IR/IMU exposure alignment; hardware-relative timestamps must not be mixed with
+UTC. After calibration, document offset sign and apply it exactly once in a
+reviewed derived input path; never rewrite raw bags. No offset key is invented
+in the current Settings schema. The repo's existing global-time source link is
+[global_timestamp_reader.cpp](https://github.com/realsenseai/librealsense/blob/v2.58.4/src/global_timestamp_reader.cpp),
+already cited in [readiness](../../docs/D435I_VIO_CALIBRATION_READINESS.md);
+it was not fetched during this network-free task.
+
+## Limitations and remaining work
+
+Mac synthetic checks prove input association and artifact consistency only.
+No librealsense/OpenCV development headers were found in the checked standard
+Mac include roots, so recorder/driver SDK compilation and OpenCV FileStorage
+parsing remain OPEN. Pi libraries, exact SDK bag semantics, backpressure/EOF,
+SIGINT, all-frame reconciliation, image quality, timing/calibration, VIO behavior
+and live throughput need future validation. Existing historical evidence and
+project gate docs are unchanged. This folder supersedes the earlier proposed
+EuRoC conversion only as a **review proposal for this ticket**, not an approved
+project-wide data-format decision or an N3 bypass.
diff --git a/experiments/2026-10-13-n4b-d435i-prep/test_d435i_input.cpp b/experiments/2026-10-13-n4b-d435i-prep/test_d435i_input.cpp
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..3521557693393ab715674d3e10c5ff8361cafaf3
--- /dev/null
+++ b/experiments/2026-10-13-n4b-d435i-prep/test_d435i_input.cpp
@@ -0,0 +1,42 @@
+// OFFLINE/SYNTHETIC ONLY. These fixtures cannot qualify SDK timing or hardware.
+#include "d435i_input.h"
+#include <cassert>
+#include <iostream>
+#include <limits>
+
+template<class F> void rejects(F fn) {
+    bool rejected=false;
+    try { fn(); } catch (const std::runtime_error&) { rejected=true; }
+    assert(rejected);
+}
+int main() {
+    const wbr::Sample a{1.0,{0,2,-2}}, b{1.01,{10,4,2}};
+    const auto m=wbr::interpolate(a,b,1.005);
+    assert(std::abs(m.x-5)<1e-10 && std::abs(m.y-3)<1e-10 && std::abs(m.z)<1e-10);
+    rejects([&]{ wbr::interpolate(a,b,1.02); });
+    rejects([&]{ wbr::interpolate(a,a,1.0); });
+    wbr::Input input;
+    input.gyro({0.999,{1,2,3}});
+    input.accel(a); input.accel(b);
+    input.gyro({1.003,{1,2,3}}); input.gyro({1.007,{4,5,6}});
+    input.trim_prefix(); assert(input.prefix_gyro==1);
+    assert(input.before_coverage(1.001));
+    assert(!input.ready(1.008)); // Requires first gyro >= camera time, not stale propagation.
+    const auto first=input.take(1.005);
+    assert(first.size()==2 && first[0].t==1.003 && first[1].t==1.007);
+    assert(std::abs(first[0].accel.x-3)<1e-10);
+    assert(std::abs(first[1].accel.x-7)<1e-10);
+    input.gyro({1.012,{7,8,9}});
+    assert(!input.ready(1.011)); // Future accel bracket must arrive.
+    input.accel({1.02,{20,6,6}});
+    const auto second=input.take(1.011);
+    assert(second.size()==1 && second[0].t==1.012); // Endpoint sent once, no duplicate.
+    assert(std::abs(second[0].accel.x-12)<1e-10);
+    rejects([&]{ input.take(1.1); });
+    rejects([&]{ input.gyro({1.012,{0,0,0}}); });
+    rejects([&]{ input.accel({1.015,{0,0,0}}); });
+    rejects([&]{ input.gyro({1.1,{0,0,0}}); }); // Interior gap.
+    rejects([&]{ input.gyro({1.015,{std::numeric_limits<double>::quiet_NaN(),0,0}}); });
+    rejects([&]{ input.gyro({std::numeric_limits<double>::infinity(),{0,0,0}}); });
+    std::cout << "OFFLINE/SYNTHETIC: interpolation, ordering, gaps and boundary fixtures completed; hardware OPEN\n";
+}

diff --git a/experiments/2026-10-13-n4b-d435i-prep/D435i_317422076650_stereo_inertial.yaml b/experiments/2026-10-13-n4b-d435i-prep/D435i_317422076650_stereo_inertial.yaml
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..bef4a5f196872e1801b83565050bb68ff1e731ba
--- /dev/null
+++ b/experiments/2026-10-13-n4b-d435i-prep/D435i_317422076650_stereo_inertial.yaml
@@ -0,0 +1,62 @@
+%YAML:1.0
+# Status: OPEN. Runnable development candidate; no N4 qualification.
+# MEASURED SDK factory readback: ../2026-10-13-pi5-env-snapshot/rs_calibration_new_unit.txt
+# SDK serial 317422076650, firmware 5.17.3.10, BMI085, 2026-10-13.
+# See calibration_notes.md for provenance, transform math and upstream comparison.
+File.version: "1.0"
+Camera.type: "Rectified"
+
+# Both IR1 and IR2 640x480 Y8 have identical MEASURED SDK intrinsics and
+# Brown Conrady coefficients [0,0,0,0,0]. Rectified schema uses Camera1 only.
+Camera1.fx: 386.953308105469
+Camera1.fy: 386.953308105469
+Camera1.cx: 321.034301757812
+Camera1.cy: 241.040130615234
+# Positive baseline magnitude, from IR1 -> IR2 translation [-b,0,0] metres.
+Stereo.b: 0.049912553280592
+Camera.width: 640
+Camera.height: 480
+# ASSUMED operating choice; supported by enumeration, delivery not measured.
+Camera.fps: 30
+Camera.RGB: 1
+Stereo.ThDepth: 40.0
+
+# Actual ORB convention: camera -> IMU/body, p_b = T_b_c1 * p_c1.
+# SDK IR1 -> Gyro/Accel readback, NOT its inverse. Values read are MEASURED;
+# physical IMU alignment is INFERRED nominal mechanical/CAD, not calibrated.
+# The upstream RealSense matrix's body-to-camera comment is misleading.
+IMU.T_b_c1: !!opencv-matrix
+   rows: 4
+   cols: 4
+   dt: f
+   data: [1.0, 0.0, 0.0, -0.00552000012248755,
+          0.0, 1.0, 0.0,  0.00510000018402934,
+          0.0, 0.0, 1.0,  0.011739999987185,
+          0.0, 0.0, 0.0,  1.0]
+IMU.InsertKFsWhenLost: 0
+# SOURCE-SUPPORTED upstream RealSense_D435i.yaml; ASSUMED for this BMI085 unit.
+# Continuous-time densities; do not pre-discretize. Allan variance is required
+# for N4 qualification. IMU intrinsic calibration and time offset are UNKNOWN.
+IMU.NoiseGyro: 1e-3
+IMU.NoiseAcc: 1e-2
+IMU.GyroWalk: 1e-6
+IMU.AccWalk: 1e-4
+# Gyro-grid combined input, with bracketed accel/100 interpolation. Not raw accel Hz.
+IMU.Frequency: 200.0
+
+# SOURCE-SUPPORTED upstream tuning; ASSUMED suitability for this experiment.
+ORBextractor.nFeatures: 1250
+ORBextractor.scaleFactor: 1.2
+ORBextractor.nLevels: 8
+ORBextractor.iniThFAST: 20
+ORBextractor.minThFAST: 7
+Viewer.KeyFrameSize: 0.05
+Viewer.KeyFrameLineWidth: 1.0
+Viewer.GraphLineWidth: 0.9
+Viewer.PointSize: 2.0
+Viewer.CameraSize: 0.08
+Viewer.CameraLineWidth: 3.0
+Viewer.ViewpointX: 0.0
+Viewer.ViewpointY: -0.7
+Viewer.ViewpointZ: -3.5
+Viewer.ViewpointF: 500.0
diff --git a/experiments/2026-10-13-n4b-d435i-prep/_proposed_driver.cc b/experiments/2026-10-13-n4b-d435i-prep/_proposed_driver.cc
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..237921a5b1f6098ea5523b13bdd34f8704cd1181
--- /dev/null
+++ b/experiments/2026-10-13-n4b-d435i-prep/_proposed_driver.cc
@@ -0,0 +1,197 @@
+#include <System.h>
+#include <opencv2/imgproc.hpp>
+#include "d435i_input.h"
+#include "d435i_rs.h"
+#include <csignal>
+#include <condition_variable>
+#include <filesystem>
+#include <fstream>
+#include <functional>
+#include <iostream>
+#include <mutex>
+
+namespace { volatile std::sig_atomic_t running=1;
+void stop(int) { running=0; }
+struct Image { cv::Mat left, right; double t; };
+struct Cleanup { std::function<void()> fn; ~Cleanup() { if (fn) fn(); } };
+}
+
+int main(int argc, char** argv) {
+    if (argc<3) {
+        std::cerr << "Usage: stereo_inertial_realsense_D435i VOCAB YAML [trajectory_name] "
+                     "[--bag FILE] [--no-viewer]\n";
+        return 2;
+    }
+    std::string bag, name="wbr";
+    bool viewer=true, named=false;
+    for (int i=3; i<argc; ++i) {
+        const std::string arg(argv[i]);
+        if (arg=="--no-viewer") viewer=false;
+        else if (arg=="--bag" && i+1<argc && bag.empty()) bag=argv[++i];
+        else if (arg.rfind("--",0)!=0 && !named) { name=arg; named=true; }
+        else { std::cerr << "Invalid argument: " << arg << '\n'; return 2; }
+    }
+    if (name.empty() || name.find_first_not_of("abcdefghijklmnopqrstuvwxyzABCDEFGHIJKLMNOPQRSTUVWXYZ0123456789_-")!=std::string::npos) {
+        std::cerr << "trajectory name must contain only letters, digits, underscore or hyphen\n";
+        return 2;
+    }
+    for (const auto& suffix : {"_timestamps.csv", "_tracking.csv", "_CameraTrajectory.txt", "_KeyFrameTrajectory.txt"})
+        if (std::filesystem::exists(name+suffix)) {
+            std::cerr << "Refusing existing output: " << name+suffix << '\n'; return 2;
+        }
+    std::signal(SIGINT,stop);
+    std::signal(SIGTERM,stop);
+    try {
+        std::ofstream audit(name+"_timestamps.csv"), tracking(name+"_tracking.csv");
+        if (!audit || !tracking) throw std::runtime_error("cannot create output logs");
+        wbr::stamp_header(audit);
+        tracking << "image_s,state,imu_initialized,imu_samples,track_ms\n" << std::setprecision(17);
+        rs2::pipeline pipe;
+        rs2::config cfg;
+        wbr::streams(cfg);
+        if (bag.empty()) cfg.enable_device("317422076650");
+        else cfg.enable_device_from_file(bag, false); // No repeat and no physical-device query.
+        const auto resolved=cfg.resolve(pipe);
+        wbr::verify(resolved, std::cout);
+        if (bag.empty()) wbr::live_options(resolved.get_device(), std::cout);
+        auto playback=resolved.get_device().as<rs2::playback>();
+        if (!bag.empty()) {
+            if (!playback) throw std::runtime_error("file did not resolve to playback");
+            playback.set_real_time(false); // Set before callbacks start; timestamps stay recorded.
+        }
+        // Load vocabulary before acquisition: startup cannot overflow the input buffer.
+        ORB_SLAM3::System SLAM(argv[1],argv[2],ORB_SLAM3::System::IMU_STEREO,viewer,0,name);
+        std::mutex mutex;
+        std::condition_variable changed;
+        wbr::Input input;
+        std::deque<Image> images;
+        bool eof=false, played=false, closing=false;
+        std::string error;
+        int domain=-1;
+        double last_image=-INFINITY;
+        unsigned long received=0, processed=0, prefix=0, tail=0;
+        auto check_domain = [&](const rs2::frame& f) {
+            const int d=static_cast<int>(f.get_frame_timestamp_domain());
+            if (domain==-1) domain=d;
+            if (domain!=d) throw std::runtime_error("mixed/changing timestamp domains; preserve and investigate");
+        };
+        if (playback) playback.set_status_changed_callback([&](rs2_playback_status status) {
+            std::lock_guard<std::mutex> lock(mutex);
+            if (status==RS2_PLAYBACK_STATUS_PLAYING) played=true;
+            if (status==RS2_PLAYBACK_STATUS_STOPPED && played) eof=true;
+            changed.notify_all();
+        });
+        auto callback = [&](const rs2::frame& f) {
+            std::unique_lock<std::mutex> lock(mutex);
+            if (closing || !error.empty()) return;
+            try {
+                if (auto fs=f.as<rs2::frameset>()) {
+                    const auto l=fs.get_infrared_frame(1), r=fs.get_infrared_frame(2);
+                    if (!l || !r) throw std::runtime_error("incomplete stereo frameset");
+                    wbr::stamp(audit,l); wbr::stamp(audit,r);
+                    check_domain(l); check_domain(r);
+                    const double t=l.get_timestamp()*1e-3;
+                    if (!std::isfinite(t) || t<=last_image || std::abs(l.get_timestamp()-r.get_timestamp())>1.0)
+                        throw std::runtime_error("invalid/repeated stereo stamps or >1 ms pair skew");
+                    last_image=t; ++received;
+                    if (images.size()>=8) {
+                        // Non-real-time playback waits for processing. Live overload fails explicitly.
+                        if (!playback || !changed.wait_for(lock,std::chrono::seconds(10),[&]{
+                            return images.size()<8 || closing || !error.empty() || !running;
+                        })) throw std::runtime_error("image queue overflow/backpressure timeout");
+                    }
+                    if (closing || !error.empty() || !running) return;
+                    // Own pixels and honor row stride; no dangling SDK data pointers.
+                    images.push_back({cv::Mat(l.get_height(),l.get_width(),CV_8U,
+                        const_cast<void*>(l.get_data()),l.get_stride_in_bytes()).clone(),
+                        cv::Mat(r.get_height(),r.get_width(),CV_8U,
+                        const_cast<void*>(r.get_data()),r.get_stride_in_bytes()).clone(),t});
+                } else if (auto m=f.as<rs2::motion_frame>()) {
+                    wbr::stamp(audit,m); check_domain(m);
+                    const auto v=m.get_motion_data();
+                    const wbr::Sample sample{m.get_timestamp()*1e-3,{v.x,v.y,v.z}};
+                    if (m.get_profile().stream_type()==RS2_STREAM_GYRO) input.gyro(sample);
+                    else if (m.get_profile().stream_type()==RS2_STREAM_ACCEL) input.accel(sample);
+                }
+                changed.notify_all();
+            } catch (const std::exception& e) { error=e.what(); changed.notify_all(); }
+        };
+        bool started=false;
+        Cleanup cleanup{[&] {
+            { std::lock_guard<std::mutex> lock(mutex); closing=true; changed.notify_all(); }
+            if (started) {
+                try { pipe.stop(); }
+                catch (const std::exception& e) { std::cerr << "pipeline stop error: " << e.what() << '\n'; }
+            }
+            SLAM.Shutdown();
+        }};
+        pipe.start(cfg,callback);
+        started=true;
+        bool first=true, initialized=false;
+        auto progress=std::chrono::steady_clock::now();
+        while (running && !SLAM.isShutDown()) {
+            Image image;
+            std::vector<wbr::Combined> samples;
+            {
+                std::unique_lock<std::mutex> lock(mutex);
+                changed.wait_for(lock,std::chrono::milliseconds(100));
+                if (!error.empty()) break;
+                if (first) input.trim_prefix();
+                if (images.empty()) {
+                    if (eof) break;
+                } else if (first && input.before_coverage(images.front().t)) {
+                    images.pop_front(); ++prefix; changed.notify_all(); continue;
+                } else if (input.ready(images.front().t)) {
+                    image=images.front(); images.pop_front();
+                    samples=input.take(image.t); changed.notify_all();
+                } else if (eof) {
+                    tail=images.size(); images.clear(); break;
+                }
+                if (samples.empty()) {
+                    if (std::chrono::steady_clock::now()-progress>std::chrono::seconds(5)) {
+                        error="no processable stereo/IMU coverage for 5 s"; break;
+                    }
+                    continue;
+                }
+            }
+            first=false;
+            std::vector<ORB_SLAM3::IMU::Point> imu;
+            for (const auto& s : samples)
+                imu.emplace_back(s.accel.x,s.accel.y,s.accel.z,s.gyro.x,s.gyro.y,s.gyro.z,s.t);
+            const float scale=SLAM.GetImageScale();
+            if (scale!=1.f) {
+                cv::resize(image.left,image.left,cv::Size(),scale,scale);
+                cv::resize(image.right,image.right,cv::Size(),scale,scale);
+            }
+            const auto start=std::chrono::steady_clock::now();
+            SLAM.TrackStereo(image.left,image.right,image.t,imu);
+            const auto end=std::chrono::steady_clock::now();
+            const bool now_initialized=SLAM.GetTimeFromIMUInit()>0;
+            if (now_initialized && !initialized) std::cout << "IMU initialized (System.GetTimeFromIMUInit > 0)\n";
+            initialized=now_initialized;
+            tracking << image.t << ',' << SLAM.GetTrackingState() << ',' << initialized << ','
+                     << imu.size() << ',' << std::chrono::duration<double,std::milli>(end-start).count() << '\n';
+            if (!tracking) { std::lock_guard<std::mutex> lock(mutex); error="tracking audit write failed"; break; }
+            ++processed; progress=end;
+        }
+        cleanup.fn(); // Wake blocked callbacks before stop; EOF is drained above.
+        cleanup.fn={};
+        audit.flush(); tracking.flush();
+        std::cout << "received=" << received << " processed=" << processed
+                  << " prefix_images=" << prefix << " prefix_gyro=" << input.prefix_gyro
+                  << " uncovered_tail_images=" << tail << " pending_images=" << images.size() << '\n';
+        if (!error.empty() || !audit || !tracking || !processed) {
+            std::cerr << "OPEN: input/run error: " << error << '\n'; return 1;
+        }
+        // The pinned exporter dereferences the largest map; avoid empty-map calls.
+        if (SLAM.GetTrackedMapPoints().empty()) {
+            std::cerr << "OPEN: no tracked map points at shutdown; inspect logs\n"; return 1;
+        }
+        SLAM.SaveTrajectoryEuRoC(name+"_CameraTrajectory.txt"); // Also prints atlas map count.
+        SLAM.SaveKeyFrameTrajectoryEuRoC(name+"_KeyFrameTrajectory.txt");
+        std::cout << "OPEN: run completed; inspect initialization, tracking and provenance\n";
+        return 0;
+    } catch (const std::exception& e) {
+        std::cerr << "OPEN: driver error: " << e.what() << '\n'; return 1;
+    }
+}
diff --git a/experiments/2026-10-13-n4b-d435i-prep/calibration_notes.md b/experiments/2026-10-13-n4b-d435i-prep/calibration_notes.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..20bf41fd171248ebbb54a13b8462f48e77ea4294
--- /dev/null
+++ b/experiments/2026-10-13-n4b-d435i-prep/calibration_notes.md
@@ -0,0 +1,149 @@
+# Configuration review — OPEN
+
+This is a runnable development candidate for SDK serial **317422076650**, firmware
+**5.17.3.10**, IMU **BMI085**. It does not qualify N4. All hardware, timing,
+calibration, offline VIO and live VIO conclusions remain **OPEN**.
+
+## Sources and classifications
+
+- **M — MEASURED readback:** [2026-10-13 factory enumeration](../2026-10-13-pi5-env-snapshot/rs_calibration_new_unit.txt),
+  produced by `rs-enumerate-devices -c`. This classification describes observed
+  SDK values, not a new independent optical or inertial calibration experiment.
+- **U — SOURCE-SUPPORTED:** pinned [RealSense_D435i.yaml](../../third_party/ORB_SLAM3/Examples/Stereo-Inertial/RealSense_D435i.yaml),
+  commit `4452a3c4ab75b1cde34e5505a36ec3f9edcdc4c4`.
+- **S — SOURCE-SUPPORTED:** the same commit's [Settings.cc](../../third_party/ORB_SLAM3/src/Settings.cc),
+  [ImuTypes.cc](../../third_party/ORB_SLAM3/src/ImuTypes.cc),
+  [Frame.cc](../../third_party/ORB_SLAM3/src/Frame.cc) and
+  [EuRoC.yaml](../../third_party/ORB_SLAM3/Examples/Stereo-Inertial/EuRoC.yaml).
+- **A — ASSUMED:** an operating/tuning choice for this unit, subject to measurement.
+
+The SDK serial is distinct from ASIC serial `327743061057`, firmware-update ID
+`327743061057`, and separately observed USB descriptor serial `327743061057`.
+The [swap addendum](../2026-10-13-pi5-env-snapshot/ADDENDUM_CAMERA_SWAP.md)
+establishes that old SDK serial `243322073847` is a different unit. Its tests and
+calibration results do not transfer.
+
+## Rectified stereo schema
+
+The new enumeration's IR1 and IR2 640×480 Y8 blocks (lines 326–334 and 414–422)
+both give `fx=fy=386.953308105469`, `cx=321.034301757812`,
+`cy=241.040130615234`, Brown Conrady coefficients `[0,0,0,0,0]`.
+These are the SDK rectified stream projections; physical lens distortion has
+not been independently measured. No second software rectification is proposed.
+
+`File.version: "1.0"`, `Camera.type: "Rectified"`, `Camera1.*` and `Stereo.b`
+follow the actual Settings parser. For Rectified, it does not read `Camera2.*`
+or distortion coefficients; identical right projection is assumed. Thus IR2
+values are documented here and in the YAML comment rather than added as unused
+keys. Do not substitute the EuRoC PinHole schema or legacy `Camera.bf`/`Tbc`.
+
+The measured SDK transform IR1→IR2 is `R=I`, `t=[-0.049912553280592,0,0] m`.
+The right camera center in left coordinates is `-R^T t=[+b,0,0]`.
+ORB wants the positive magnitude `Stereo.b=0.049912553280592 m` and computes
+`bf=fx*b≈19.31382761 pixel·m`. There is no sign reversal of disparity.
+
+## Transform direction and math
+
+Let `c1` denote the SDK left IR optical frame and `b` the SDK gyro/body frame.
+RealSense extrinsics **from A to B** act on points as
+`p_B=R_BA p_A+t_BA` in metres. The API rotation array is column-major; OpenCV
+matrix `data` is row-major. Identity rotation makes that distinction numerically
+invisible here. Keep the raw SDK IMU axes; do not additionally rotate to a ROS
+camera_link, ENU, NED or controller body convention.
+
+The new file's IR1→Gyro and IR1→Accel both give:
+
+```text
+R_bc = I
+t_bc = [-0.00552000012248755, +0.00510000018402934, +0.011739999987185] m
+T_bc = [ I  t_bc ]
+       [ 0   1  ]
+p_b = T_bc p_c1
+```
+
+Gyro↔Accel is identity with zero translation in the readback; shared physical
+alignment is still unmeasured. The reverse Gyro/Accel→IR1 readback is:
+
+```text
+T_cb = inverse(T_bc) = [ R_bc^T  -R_bc^T t_bc ]
+                      [   0          1      ]
+t_cb = [+0.00552000012248755, -0.00510000018402934, -0.011739999987185] m
+T_cb T_bc = I
+```
+
+**ORB's actual `IMU.T_b_c1` is `T_bc`: camera→body**, despite the upstream
+RealSense comment saying “Transformation from body-frame (imu) to left camera”.
+The EuRoC comment says camera→body. The executable evidence is stronger:
+`ImuTypes.cc` sets `mTcb=mTbc.inverse()` and `Frame.cc` sets
+`T_cw=T_cb*T_bw`. Therefore the YAML must use the IR1→Gyro transform directly.
+Using the reverse readback under this key would invert all three translation
+signs incorrectly. A camera-origin test gives `p_b=t_bc`; body origin maps to
+`p_c1=-t_bc`. The positive Y value corrects the upstream example's negative Y.
+
+The numbers are **MEASURED SDK readback**, while their interpretation as nominal
+mechanical/CAD geometry is **INFERRED / SOURCE-SUPPORTED**, not per-unit IMU
+alignment calibration. [Repository calibration readiness](../../docs/D435I_VIO_CALIBRATION_READINESS.md)
+documents the SDK fallback and links the official
+[librealsense parser v2.58.4](https://github.com/realsenseai/librealsense/blob/v2.58.4/src/ds/ds-calib-parsers.cpp).
+Its earlier raw fallback logs concern the old unit; the new numeric values match
+that nominal geometry. No Intel document with a mechanical-calibration quotation
+was found in the requested repository docs, and no online source was fetched.
+The SDK source URL is an existing repository citation, not a newly verified
+claim about the currently installed binary.
+
+The SDK warning reported in the ticket is **“IMU Calibration is not available”**;
+the full warning preserved for the old unit is “IMU Calibration is not available,
+default intrinsic and extrinsic will be used.” The new calibration text itself
+does not include a warning line. Preserve new raw SDK stderr during later tests
+and do not silently attribute old warning logs to this serial.
+
+New gyro/accel readback gives identity sensitivity, zero bias, zero noise
+variance and zero bias variance (lines 471–488). These are not evidence of a
+noiseless IMU. Whether `rs-imu-calibration` was ever run successfully for this
+unit is **UNKNOWN**; treat IMU intrinsics as uncalibrated until evidence resolves
+the warning/defaults. No calibration tool or firmware operation is authorized
+by this preparation. Spatial/temporal calibration and a stationary full-precision
+Allan-variance run are required before N4 qualification. Choose duration from
+the desired averaging times, normally hours rather than this 60–90 s VIO take;
+use qualified storage and a separately reviewed procedure.
+
+## Upstream versus candidate
+
+All upstream entries below are **U**. Candidate values marked **U+A** reuse
+example values as assumptions for this unit. Noise units are continuous-time
+density units, not SDK variance-array entries.
+
+| Key / quantity | Upstream RealSense_D435i.yaml | Candidate | Candidate source |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| File.version / Camera.type | `"1.0"` / `Rectified` | same | S: exact parser schema |
+| Camera1.fx / fy (px) | 382.613 / 382.613 | 386.953308105469 / same | M: IR1 640×480 |
+| Camera1.cx / cy (px) | 320.183 / 236.455 | 321.034301757812 / 241.040130615234 | M: IR1 |
+| IR2 fx/fy/cx/cy | implicit same rectified projection | same as IR1 | M: IR2; S: no Camera2 keys read |
+| Distortion | implicit ideal rectified pinhole | five zeros, omitted from schema | M: both IR blocks; S |
+| Stereo.b (m) | 0.0499585 | 0.049912553280592 | M: magnitude of IR1→IR2 t_x |
+| Camera.width / height | 640 / 480 | same | M capability; A selection |
+| Camera.fps | 30 | 30 | M capability; A choice to match example and motion |
+| Camera.RGB | 1 | 1 | U+A; ignored for Y8 |
+| Stereo.ThDepth | 40.0 | 40.0 | U+A; close threshold ≈1.9965 m |
+| IMU.T_b_c1 rotation | identity | identity | M readback; nominal physical interpretation |
+| IMU.T_b_c1 t_x (m) | -0.005 | -0.00552000012248755 | M IR1→Gyro |
+| IMU.T_b_c1 t_y (m) | -0.005 | +0.00510000018402934 | M; direction established by S |
+| IMU.T_b_c1 t_z (m) | +0.0117 | +0.011739999987185 | M IR1→Gyro |
+| IMU.InsertKFsWhenLost | 0 | 0 | U+A |
+| IMU.NoiseGyro (rad/s/√Hz) | 1e-3 | 1e-3 | U+A; Allan variance required |
+| IMU.NoiseAcc (m/s²/√Hz) | 1e-2 | 1e-2 | U+A; Allan variance required |
+| IMU.GyroWalk (rad/s²/√Hz) | 1e-6 | 1e-6 | U+A; Allan variance required |
+| IMU.AccWalk (m/s³/√Hz) | 1e-4 | 1e-4 | U+A; Allan variance required |
+| IMU.Frequency | 200.0 | 200.0 | U+A: gyro-grid input, not accel rate |
+| ORBextractor.nFeatures | 1250 | 1250 | U+A |
+| ORBextractor.scaleFactor / nLevels | 1.2 / 8 | same | U+A |
+| ORBextractor.iniThFAST / minThFAST | 20 / 7 | same | U+A |
+| Viewer.KeyFrameSize / KeyFrameLineWidth | 0.05 / 1.0 | same | U+A |
+| Viewer.GraphLineWidth / PointSize | 0.9 / 2.0 | same | U+A |
+| Viewer.CameraSize / CameraLineWidth | 0.08 / 3.0 | same | U+A |
+| Viewer.ViewpointX/Y/Z/F | 0.0 / -0.7 / -3.5 / 500.0 | same | U+A; `--no-viewer` for Pi |
+
+Noise densities are left continuous-time: the pinned tracking setup applies
+`sqrt(IMU.Frequency)` scaling to measurement noise and inverse scaling to walks.
+Do not apply that conversion twice. Bias, scale, actual sample rates and
+camera–IMU time offset remain **UNKNOWN**, rather than assumed calibrated to zero.
diff --git a/experiments/2026-10-13-n4b-d435i-prep/d435i_input.h b/experiments/2026-10-13-n4b-d435i-prep/d435i_input.h
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..88fe9cff87feadc3e4b9c703c6f40293b03d8360
--- /dev/null
+++ b/experiments/2026-10-13-n4b-d435i-prep/d435i_input.h
@@ -0,0 +1,64 @@
+// Status: OPEN. Pure input association for synthetic checks and the proposed driver.
+#pragma once
+#include <cmath>
+#include <deque>
+#include <stdexcept>
+#include <vector>
+
+namespace wbr {
+struct Vec3 { double x, y, z; };
+struct Sample { double t; Vec3 v; };
+struct Combined { double t; Vec3 accel, gyro; };
+inline Vec3 interpolate(const Sample& a, const Sample& b, double t) {
+    if (!(a.t < b.t && a.t <= t && t <= b.t))
+        throw std::runtime_error("accel requires strictly ordered brackets; no extrapolation");
+    const double u = (t-a.t)/(b.t-a.t);
+    return {a.v.x+u*(b.v.x-a.v.x), a.v.y+u*(b.v.y-a.v.y),
+            a.v.z+u*(b.v.z-a.v.z)};
+}
+class Input {
+    std::deque<Sample> accel_, gyro_;
+    double last_accel_ = -INFINITY, last_gyro_ = -INFINITY;
+    static void append(std::deque<Sample>& q, double& last, Sample s) {
+        if (!std::isfinite(s.t) || !std::isfinite(s.v.x) || !std::isfinite(s.v.y) ||
+            !std::isfinite(s.v.z) || s.t <= last)
+            throw std::runtime_error("nonfinite or duplicate/backward IMU sample");
+        // Development guard only; does not replace the N2 timing thresholds.
+        if (std::isfinite(last) && s.t-last > 0.05)
+            throw std::runtime_error("IMU gap exceeds development guard of 50 ms");
+        if (q.size() >= 4096) throw std::runtime_error("IMU queue overflow");
+        last = s.t;
+        q.push_back(s);
+    }
+public:
+    unsigned long prefix_gyro = 0;
+    void accel(Sample s) { append(accel_, last_accel_, s); }
+    void gyro(Sample s) { append(gyro_, last_gyro_, s); }
+    void trim_prefix() {
+        while (!accel_.empty() && !gyro_.empty() && gyro_.front().t < accel_.front().t) {
+            gyro_.pop_front(); ++prefix_gyro;
+        }
+    }
+    bool before_coverage(double t) const {
+        return !gyro_.empty() && t < gyro_.front().t;
+    }
+    bool ready(double t) const {
+        if (accel_.size() < 2 || gyro_.empty()) return false;
+        for (const auto& g : gyro_) if (g.t >= t)
+            return accel_.front().t <= gyro_.front().t && accel_.back().t >= g.t;
+        return false;
+    }
+    std::vector<Combined> take(double t) {
+        if (!ready(t)) throw std::runtime_error("missing trailing gyro/accel coverage");
+        std::vector<Combined> result;
+        do {
+            const auto g = gyro_.front(); gyro_.pop_front();
+            while (accel_.size() > 2 && accel_[1].t <= g.t) accel_.pop_front();
+            result.push_back({g.t, interpolate(accel_[0], accel_[1], g.t), g.v});
+        } while (result.back().t < t);
+        // Include the first gyro >= image stamp once. ORB retains that endpoint
+        // internally for the next preintegration interval (Tracking.cc).
+        return result;
+    }
+};
+} // namespace wbr
diff --git a/experiments/2026-10-13-n4b-d435i-prep/d435i_record.cpp b/experiments/2026-10-13-n4b-d435i-prep/d435i_record.cpp
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..d9efc1d6bbde2f222b3a959f28337cf9d9939a4a
--- /dev/null
+++ b/experiments/2026-10-13-n4b-d435i-prep/d435i_record.cpp
@@ -0,0 +1,80 @@
+// Status: OPEN. Future Pi-only recorder; no camera execution or SDK build on Mac.
+#include "d435i_rs.h"
+#include <csignal>
+#include <filesystem>
+#include <fstream>
+#include <iostream>
+#include <mutex>
+#include <thread>
+
+namespace { volatile std::sig_atomic_t running = 1;
+void stop(int) { running = 0; } }
+
+int main(int argc, char** argv) {
+    if (argc != 3) {
+        std::cerr << "Usage: d435i_record NEW_OUTPUT_DIRECTORY SECONDS (1..120)\n";
+        return 2;
+    }
+    try {
+        std::size_t used=0;
+        const double seconds=std::stod(argv[2], &used);
+        if (used!=std::string(argv[2]).size() || !std::isfinite(seconds) || seconds<1 || seconds>120)
+            throw std::runtime_error("duration must be 1..120 seconds");
+        const std::filesystem::path dir(argv[1]);
+        if (!std::filesystem::create_directory(dir))
+            throw std::runtime_error("output directory must be new; parent must already exist");
+        std::ofstream audit(dir/"timestamps.csv");
+        if (!audit) throw std::runtime_error("cannot create timestamp audit");
+        wbr::stamp_header(audit);
+        std::signal(SIGINT, stop);
+        std::signal(SIGTERM, stop);
+        rs2::pipeline pipe;
+        rs2::config cfg;
+        wbr::streams(cfg);
+        cfg.enable_device("317422076650");
+        cfg.enable_record_to_file((dir/"stereo_imu.bag").string());
+        auto resolved=cfg.resolve(pipe);
+        wbr::verify(resolved, std::cout);
+        wbr::live_options(resolved.get_device(), std::cout);
+        std::mutex mutex;
+        std::string error;
+        unsigned long left=0, right=0, gyro=0, accel=0;
+        auto callback = [&](const rs2::frame& frame) {
+            std::lock_guard<std::mutex> lock(mutex);
+            if (!error.empty()) return;
+            try {
+                if (auto fs=frame.as<rs2::frameset>()) {
+                    for (const auto& f : fs) {
+                        wbr::stamp(audit, f);
+                        if (f.get_profile().stream_type()==RS2_STREAM_INFRARED) {
+                            if (f.get_profile().stream_index()==1) ++left;
+                            if (f.get_profile().stream_index()==2) ++right;
+                        }
+                    }
+                } else {
+                    wbr::stamp(audit, frame);
+                    if (frame.get_profile().stream_type()==RS2_STREAM_GYRO) ++gyro;
+                    if (frame.get_profile().stream_type()==RS2_STREAM_ACCEL) ++accel;
+                }
+            } catch (const std::exception& e) { error=e.what(); }
+        };
+        pipe.start(cfg, callback);
+        const auto begin=std::chrono::steady_clock::now();
+        while (running && std::chrono::duration<double>(std::chrono::steady_clock::now()-begin).count()<seconds) {
+            { std::lock_guard<std::mutex> lock(mutex); if (!error.empty()) break; }
+            std::this_thread::sleep_for(std::chrono::milliseconds(100));
+        }
+        pipe.stop(); // Normal shutdown finalizes the librealsense bag; no forced kill.
+        audit.flush();
+        std::cout << "callback counts IR1=" << left << " IR2=" << right
+                  << " gyro=" << gyro << " accel=" << accel << '\n';
+        if (!error.empty()) throw std::runtime_error(error);
+        if (!audit || !left || !right || !gyro || !accel)
+            throw std::runtime_error("missing stream or audit flush failure");
+        std::cout << "OPEN: recorded; decode/count/timing/storage qualification still required\n";
+        return 0;
+    } catch (const std::exception& e) {
+        std::cerr << "OPEN: recorder error: " << e.what() << '\n';
+        return 1;
+    }
+}
diff --git a/experiments/2026-10-13-n4b-d435i-prep/d435i_rs.h b/experiments/2026-10-13-n4b-d435i-prep/d435i_rs.h
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..e50b62911831c5eb24001c923f37b801782d20c9
--- /dev/null
+++ b/experiments/2026-10-13-n4b-d435i-prep/d435i_rs.h
@@ -0,0 +1,84 @@
+// Status: OPEN. Shared fixed stream selection and audit logging; SDK compile unverified.
+#pragma once
+#include <librealsense2/rs.hpp>
+#include <chrono>
+#include <cmath>
+#include <iomanip>
+#include <ostream>
+#include <stdexcept>
+#include <string>
+
+namespace wbr {
+inline void streams(rs2::config& cfg) {
+    cfg.disable_all_streams();
+    cfg.enable_stream(RS2_STREAM_INFRARED, 1, 640, 480, RS2_FORMAT_Y8, 30);
+    cfg.enable_stream(RS2_STREAM_INFRARED, 2, 640, 480, RS2_FORMAT_Y8, 30);
+    cfg.enable_stream(RS2_STREAM_GYRO, RS2_FORMAT_MOTION_XYZ32F, 200);
+    cfg.enable_stream(RS2_STREAM_ACCEL, RS2_FORMAT_MOTION_XYZ32F, 100);
+}
+inline void live_options(rs2::device dev, std::ostream& log) {
+    bool emitter = false;
+    for (auto sensor : dev.query_sensors()) {
+        if (sensor.supports(RS2_OPTION_EMITTER_ENABLED)) {
+            sensor.set_option(RS2_OPTION_EMITTER_ENABLED, 0);
+            if (sensor.get_option(RS2_OPTION_EMITTER_ENABLED) != 0)
+                throw std::runtime_error("emitter OFF readback failed");
+            emitter = true;
+        }
+        // Preserve current global-time and motion-correction options; log them.
+        // No persistent device/calibration changes or implicit global-time toggle.
+        for (auto option : {RS2_OPTION_GLOBAL_TIME_ENABLED, RS2_OPTION_ENABLE_MOTION_CORRECTION})
+            if (sensor.supports(option))
+                log << sensor.get_info(RS2_CAMERA_INFO_NAME) << " " << option << "="
+                    << sensor.get_option(option) << '\n';
+    }
+    if (!emitter) throw std::runtime_error("no emitter control; cannot attest OFF");
+    log << "emitter=0 (read back before streaming)\n";
+}
+inline void verify(rs2::pipeline_profile profile, std::ostream& log) {
+    const auto dev = profile.get_device();
+    if (std::string(dev.get_info(RS2_CAMERA_INFO_SERIAL_NUMBER)) != "317422076650")
+        throw std::runtime_error("wrong SDK device serial");
+    log << "SDK serial=" << dev.get_info(RS2_CAMERA_INFO_SERIAL_NUMBER)
+        << " firmware=" << dev.get_info(RS2_CAMERA_INFO_FIRMWARE_VERSION) << '\n';
+    const auto profiles = profile.get_streams();
+    if (profiles.size() != 4) throw std::runtime_error("expected exactly four streams");
+    bool left=false, right=false, gyro=false, accel=false;
+    for (auto p : profiles) {
+        log << p.stream_name() << " index=" << p.stream_index() << " format="
+            << p.format() << " fps=" << p.fps() << '\n';
+        if (p.stream_type() == RS2_STREAM_INFRARED) {
+            const auto v = p.as<rs2::video_stream_profile>();
+            if (v.width()!=640 || v.height()!=480 || p.fps()!=30 || p.format()!=RS2_FORMAT_Y8)
+                throw std::runtime_error("wrong IR profile");
+            if (p.stream_index()==1) left=true;
+            else if (p.stream_index()==2) right=true;
+        } else if (p.stream_type()==RS2_STREAM_GYRO)
+            gyro = p.fps()==200 && p.format()==RS2_FORMAT_MOTION_XYZ32F;
+        else if (p.stream_type()==RS2_STREAM_ACCEL)
+            accel = p.fps()==100 && p.format()==RS2_FORMAT_MOTION_XYZ32F;
+    }
+    if (!(left && right && gyro && accel)) throw std::runtime_error("wrong stream set");
+}
+inline void stamp_header(std::ostream& out) {
+    out << "stream,index,frame_number,sdk_ms,domain,host_steady_ns,host_utc_ns,x,y,z,exposure_us\n";
+    out << std::setprecision(17);
+}
+inline void stamp(std::ostream& out, const rs2::frame& f) {
+    const auto mono = std::chrono::duration_cast<std::chrono::nanoseconds>(
+        std::chrono::steady_clock::now().time_since_epoch()).count();
+    const auto utc = std::chrono::duration_cast<std::chrono::nanoseconds>(
+        std::chrono::system_clock::now().time_since_epoch()).count();
+    out << f.get_profile().stream_name() << ',' << f.get_profile().stream_index()
+        << ',' << f.get_frame_number() << ',' << f.get_timestamp() << ','
+        << rs2_timestamp_domain_to_string(f.get_frame_timestamp_domain()) << ',' << mono << ',' << utc;
+    if (auto m = f.as<rs2::motion_frame>()) {
+        const auto v=m.get_motion_data(); out << ',' << v.x << ',' << v.y << ',' << v.z;
+    } else out << ",,,";
+    out << ',';
+    if (f.supports_frame_metadata(RS2_FRAME_METADATA_ACTUAL_EXPOSURE))
+        out << f.get_frame_metadata(RS2_FRAME_METADATA_ACTUAL_EXPOSURE);
+    out << '\n';
+    if (!out) throw std::runtime_error("timestamp audit write failed");
+}
+} // namespace wbr
